                <pb facs="0831" n="729" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg729"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/440: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-07-09T19:00:00-04:00">July 9, 1935—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>111. Your No. 344, July 7, noon. No note has been received from the British
                    Government in regard to the Italo-Ethiopian controversy.</p>
                <p>No one speaking for the Department has made any statement of the nature of that
                    to which you refer.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
